# CVE-2026-65182, CVE-2026-65905, CVE-2026-68525 (org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core)
#
# Apache's security advisory names the fix as version 10.1.58, 11.0.25, or 9.0.121 -
# but as of this writing, NONE of those three have actually been published to Maven
# Central yet. This is confirmed by other engineers hitting the identical wall:
# https://github.com/apache/maven/issues/12746
#
# The other two "fixed" versions are not safe alternatives either:
#   - 11.0.25 requires a newer Servlet API than Spring Boot 3.5.x supports
#   - 9.0.121 uses the old javax.* namespace, incompatible with Spring Boot 3.x's jakarta.*
#
# Accepted as a temporary, tracked risk. Remove this file and re-run once
# org.apache.tomcat.embed:tomcat-embed-core:10.1.58 is actually available on Maven Central.
CVE-2026-65182
CVE-2026-65905
CVE-2026-68525
